191754","idp_filedate":1792432497000,"nhcTitle":"Off the East Coast of the United States","discussion":"A storm-force non-tropical low pressure area is located along a  frontal boundary a few hundred miles off the southeast coast of the  United States.  This low is likely to move slowly  north-northeastward over the next couple of days.  If the low  remains over the Gulf Stream and becomes detached from the front, it  could briefly acquire some subtropical cyclone characteristics  during the middle to latter portions of the week.  The system is  expected to move northeastward away from the the eastern United  States later this week, and environmental conditions are expected to  become unfavorable for development by the weekend.  Regardless of  the status of the system, high winds, coastal flooding, and  dangerous surf are expected along portions of the U.S. East Coast  during the next few days.  Please consult statements and warnings  from local National Weather Service offices and the Weather  Prediction Center for more information, along with High Seas  Forecasts and Storm Warnings issued by the National Weather Service. \n Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent. \n Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.","disturbance":1}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-91.2385073251886,7.788644882281218],[-91.20326749962497,7.854282239229881],[-91.16990127365071,7.921496105306868],[-91.13842834722487,7.990164850851819],[-91.10886842030645,8.060166846204364],[-91.08124119285446,8.131380461704136],[-91.05556636482792,8.203684067690768],[-91.03186363618588,8.276956034503893],[-91.01015270688731,8.351074732483148],[-90.99045327689124,8.425918531968161],[-90.9727850461567,8.501365803298569],[-90.95716771464271,8.577294916814003],[-90.94362098230827,8.653584242854095],[-90.93216454911241,8.73011215175848],[-90.92281811501414,8.806757013866795],[-90.91560137997247,8.883397199518665],[-90.91053404394643,8.959911079053729